    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d817">

                <pb facs="0774" n="658" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg658"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 741.8215/48.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-05-09">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 9, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>British Government objects to G. Mason, alleging incompetency. [Appointment on
                    the boundary commission.] Appointment another surveyor imperative. Boundary
                    Commission ready to proceed. Expense delay chargeable to the Liberian
                    Government. Liberian President requests me to ascertain whether Captain Young
                    may serve as Liberian Commissioner. Believe British Government would appreciate
                    such service.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Crum.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
